# Pairs with EveryAckedWriteMaterialised. A leaf that activates with no snapshot
# and an empty projection resumes reading after its persisted checkpoint instead
# of from the start of the readable WAL - the defect the -1 cold override
# (LeafReplayStartPolicy.Decide answering Cold) exists to prevent. The writes at
# or below that checkpoint are never re-read, so the leaf never materialises
# them. The spec's fairness is intact.
# SUBSUMED in this instance: the same mutant also violates the safety invariant
# ReadPositionHonest (at depth 9), which reports it first when both are checked.
# No liveness-only protocol pairing for EveryAckedWriteMaterialised was found;
# see Refinement.md. Production detectors:
# LeafReplayStartPolicyTests.An_absent_snapshot_over_an_empty_cache_replays_cold
# and BPlusLeafGrainTests.Activation_replays_from_minus_one_when_cache_starts_empty_and_no_snapshot_rehydrated.
MODULE: EveryAckedWriteMaterialisedColdStartResumesFromCheckpoint
TARGET: EveryAckedWriteMaterialised
CLASS: Temporal
SUMMARY: a cold activation resumes after its persisted checkpoint over an empty projection
PERTURBS: Activate

--- FIND
       ELSE /\ cache' = [cache EXCEPT ![l] = {}]
            /\ rp' = [rp EXCEPT ![l] = -1]
--- REPLACE
       ELSE /\ cache' = [cache EXCEPT ![l] = {}]
\* MUTATION: no cold override; the replay starts after the checkpoint.
            /\ rp' = [rp EXCEPT ![l] = durCp[l]]
--- END